<p>unaudited historical Statements of Operations has been adjusted to reflect pro forma earnings per share for the twelve month period ended December 31, 1995, by dividing pro forma income by the weighted average number of common and common equivalent shares deemed to be outstanding.  Net income has been adjusted to pro forma net income by reflecting the tax that would have been paid by the Company if it had been subject to income tax for the full period, assuming a 40.0% effective tax rate.</p>
<p>(2) The Company believes the above presentation of historical per share information may not be meaningful because of the difficulty of comparing the Company to its predecessor entities. Therefore, this presentation shows earnings per share for the twelve month period ended December 31, 1995 as if certain adjustments, detailed in the Company's secondary public offering registration statement on Form S-1 dated March 27, 1996, were made to historical net income to give effect to the IPO and related business combination. (3) The weighted average number of common and common equivalent shares outstanding has been adjusted to a three-for-two stocksplit effective July 9, 1996.</p>
